+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links in Zip and Squashfs archives are skipped unless you use
+`--links` (or `-l`). When some are skipped, rclone logs a notice which
+names the flag.
+
+With `--links`, each symbolic link is listed as a file with the
+`.rclonelink` suffix. Its size is the length of its target, and reading
+it returns the target path. So `rclone copy --links` recreates the link
+on a local destination.
+
+A link is only listed if its target is relative, contains no `..`
+element, `\` or `:`, and is at most 4096 bytes long. It is also skipped
+if another entry would take its name on a local destination, such as a
+directory of the same name.
+
+A local destination turns a file whose name ends in `.rclonelink` into a
+link to its contents. So under `--links` such a file is only listed if
+its contents are a safe target by the same rules, and is otherwise
+skipped. This stops a copy from creating a link which points outside its
+destination.
+
